1
00:00:00,728 --> 00:00:03,688
(Sheldon:)-It appears to be a Lord of the Rings ring.
LEONARD: Oh.

2
00:00:03,856 --> 00:00:06,026
(Raj:)It's even got the Elvish engraving on it.

3
00:00:06,192 --> 00:00:07,362
(Sheldon:)It's not Elvish.

4
00:00:07,526 --> 00:00:11,616
(Sheldon:)It's the language of Mordor
written in Elvish script.

5
00:00:12,365 --> 00:00:15,115
"One ring to rule them all."

6
00:00:15,284 --> 00:00:17,324
"One ring to find them."

7
00:00:17,495 --> 00:00:19,915
"One ring to bring them all."

8
00:00:20,206 --> 00:00:23,206
"And in the darkness, bind them."

9
00:00:25,378 --> 00:00:27,708
(Raj:)Holy crap, are we nerdy.

10
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,880
(Howard:)So I was doing some checking
on the ring....

11
00:00:32,051 --> 00:00:35,011
(Raj:)Hold on. Sheldon,
is there ketchup on that table?

12
00:00:35,179 --> 00:00:38,019
(Sheldon:)Yes, there is. Oh, here's a fun fact.

13
00:00:38,182 --> 00:00:40,562
(Sheldon:)Ketchup started out as a general term
for sauce...

14
00:00:40,726 --> 00:00:44,066
...typically made of mushrooms
or fish brine with herbs and spices.

15
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:47,730
(Sheldon:)Some popular early main ingredients
included blueberry, anchovy...

16
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:51,240
(Sheldon:)...oyster, kidney bean and grape.

17
00:00:53,197 --> 00:00:55,367
(Raj:)No, that's okay, I'll get it.

18
00:00:55,741 --> 00:00:58,741
(Howard:)Listen, I was looking at the ring
and it seemed a little weird.

19
00:00:58,911 --> 00:01:00,411
(Howard:)No copyright notice on it.

